 # H10 fixture · browser activation trap
 
-This renamed Web plugin is valid on the host side but its browser bundle still
-registers a legacy identity. Exam material only — do not publish (`"private": true`).
+A renamed Web plugin. The host half mounts through `dsh.bundle.patch` /
+`cordis.patch.yml`; the browser half is declared by `dsh.client` and built from
+`client.js`.
+
+The browser bundle registers the current package identity (`Entry name ==
+package name`) and keeps the legacy identity, so a page that still serves the
+pre-rename row resolves the same bundle. Both ids are declared: `dsh.client.legacyIds`
+asks the host to compose a module-table alias row for the legacy id, and the
+bundle registers that id only when the served boot graph carries it. On a host
+that has no alias support the legacy row is never composed and the registration
+is skipped, so the plugin still activates under its current identity; the
+host-side support this entry point needs is carried by `patches/`.
+
+Exam material only — do not publish (`"private": true`).
