+# Harness patches carried by this plugin
+
+`0001-client-modules-legacy-bundle-ids.patch` is a proposal against
+`@deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness` at tag `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`. It is the host-side
+half of this plugin's documented legacy browser identity: without it the host
+never composes the legacy row, so the bundle's second registration can never be
+reached (see `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/client-bundle-legacy-ids/report.md`,
+which is the upstream discussion draft for this change).
+
+The plugin does not depend on the patch to activate: `dsh.client.legacyIds` is
+ignored by hosts that do not know it, and the bundle registers the legacy id
+only when the served boot graph carries that row.
+
+## Apply
+
+From a clean checkout of the harness at the tag above:
+
+```sh
+git checkout dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2
+git apply /path/to/0001-client-modules-legacy-bundle-ids.patch
+```
+
+The patch touches the client-modules source and its docs (7 files, no
+generated artifacts, no lockfile). It does not include the vitest specs or the
+`packages/client/modules/README.zh.md` translation, which the upstream
+contribution workflow owns.
+
+## What it changes
+
+- `dsh.client.legacyIds: string[]` in a package manifest, validated by the scan.
+- One module-table alias row (`aliasOf`) per declared id, sharing the package
+  bundle URL and revision, added to the owner's startup batch, and excluded from
+  the Cordis plugin-entry view.
+- Host read APIs (`clientPath`, `artifactBaseline`, `rebuilt`) resolve alias ids
+  to the owning record; rebuild notifications name the package row.
+- Browser `invalidate` drops every id one bundle registers (the package row plus
+  its alias rows), and the boot-manifest parser rejects malformed alias rows.
+- Docs: `docs/subsystems/client-modules.md`, `packages/client/AGENTS.md`,
+  `packages/client/modules/README.md`.
+
+## Verify
+
+The plugin's own check (`../.dsh-migrate/checks/legacy-ids.check.mjs`) runs the
+patched source with Node's type stripping and the installed alpha.2 cordis:
+
+```sh
+node --experimental-transform-types .dsh-migrate/checks/legacy-ids.check.mjs
+```
+
+It fails on an unpatched host (`legacy id becomes an alias row`) and passes with
+the patch applied.
